#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1445 expect=noViolation domain=VS
#note "Rows 1/2: two VSLOBXFL='Y' records for the same subject/VSTESTCD but different VSPOS (SITTING vs STANDING) -> --POS IS part of this rule's assessment key (unlike FDA-SD1439's), so the tuples are distinct and nothing fires. Rows 3/4: same key, only row 3 flagged 'Y' -> clean."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset VS class=FINDINGS
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
col VSPOS    type=Char label="Vital Signs Position of Subject"
col VSLOBXFL type=Char label="Last Observation Before Exposure Flag"
---
S1 | VS | S1-001 | 1 | SYSBP | SITTING  | Y
S1 | VS | S1-001 | 2 | SYSBP | STANDING | Y
S1 | VS | S1-001 | 3 | TEMP  | SITTING  | Y
S1 | VS | S1-001 | 4 | TEMP  | SITTING  |
